292a|a|Given to, or evincing, thrift; characterized by economy and good menegement of property; sparing; frugal. ; Thriving by industry and frugality; prosperous in the acquisition of worldly goods; increasing in wealth; as, a thrifty farmer or mechanic. ; Growing rapidly or vigorously; thriving; as, a thrifty plant or colt. ; Secured by thrift; well husbanded. ; Well appearing; looking or being in good condition; becoming.	e:19lo,69,3~19lo,69,3
292b|n|A warbling; a trill. ; A drill. See 3d Drill, 1. ; A sensation as of being thrilled; a tremulous excitement; as, a thrill of horror; a thrill of joy.	n:19qu,103,8~19qu,103,8
