292j|n|To prosper by industry, economy, and good management of property; to increase in goods and estate; as, a farmer thrives by good husbandry. ; To prosper in any business; to have increase or success. ; To increase in bulk or stature; to grow vigorously or luxuriantly, as a plant; to flourish; as, young cattle thrive in rich pastures; trees thrive in a good soil.	n:29wu,110,2~29wu,110,2
