2949|n|Thrist. ; A violent push or driving, as with a pointed weapon moved in the direction of its length, or with the hand or foot, or with any instrument; a stab; -- a word much used as a term of fencing. ; An attack; an assault. ; The force or pressure of one part of a construction against other parts; especially (Arch.), a horizontal or diagonal outward pressure, as of an arch against its abutments, or of rafters against the wall which support them. ; The breaking down of the roof of a gallery under its superincumbent weight.	a:1bgw,76,30;x78,45,6~1bgw,76,30;x78,45,6
